{
  "id": "09296_pakuru",
  "headword": "パクる",
  "reading": "ぱくる",
  "part_of_speech": "godan verb",
  "gloss": "to steal; to copy; to plagiarize",
  "definitions": [
    {
      "sense_number": 1,
      "gloss": "to steal; to swipe",
      "explanation": "To take something without permission (slang)."
    },
    {
      "sense_number": 2,
      "gloss": "to copy; to plagiarize; to rip off",
      "explanation": "To copy someone's work, ideas, or style without credit."
    }
  ],
  "examples": [
    {
      "id": "09296_pakuru_ex1",
      "japanese": "{財布|さいふ}をパクられた。",
      "english": "My wallet got stolen.",
      "has_audio": false,
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "09296_pakuru_ex2",
      "japanese": "{店|みせ}で{菓子|かし}をパクった。",
      "english": "I swiped some snacks from the store.",
      "has_audio": false,
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "09296_pakuru_ex3",
      "japanese": "{自転車|じてんしゃ}をパクられて{困|こま}っている。",
      "english": "I'm in trouble because my bicycle was stolen.",
      "has_audio": false,
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "09296_pakuru_ex4",
      "japanese": "アイデアをパクるな。",
      "english": "Don't steal my idea.",
      "has_audio": false,
      "sense_numbers": [
        2
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "09296_pakuru_ex5",
      "japanese": "あのデザインは{完全|かんぜん}にパクリだ。",
      "english": "That design is a complete rip-off.",
      "has_audio": false,
      "sense_numbers": [
        2
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "09296_pakuru_ex6",
      "japanese": "{有名|ゆうめい}な{曲|きょく}をパクったと{言|い}われている。",
      "english": "They say it plagiarized a famous song.",
      "has_audio": false,
      "sense_numbers": [
        2
      ]
    }
  ],
  "notes": "パクる is slang that may come from the onomatopoeia パクパク (munching/gobbling sound), suggesting \"gobbling up\" something. It's also sometimes written as ぱくる in hiragana.\n\nREGISTER:\nThis is casual slang. Avoid using it in formal situations. For sense 1, use {盗|ぬす}む. For sense 2, use {盗作|とうさく}する or {模倣|もほう}する.\n\nRELATED NOUN:\nパクリ means \"a rip-off\" or \"plagiarism\" (noun form).\n\nCOMMON PATTERNS:\n- ～をパクる: to steal/copy something\n- ～からパクる: to steal/copy from someone",
